WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:03.090
Hi, Mystery Recapped here.

00:00:03.090 --> 00:00:09.549
Today I am going to explain a short sci-fi
drama film called “High Maintenance.”

00:00:09.549 --> 00:00:10.940
Spoilers ahead!

00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:17.300
Watch out and take care!

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:23.150
At the beginning of the movie, we are introduced
to a man and his wife namely; Paul and Jane.

00:00:23.150 --> 00:00:26.240
The two are dining on a fine evening in their
house.

00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:31.590
The table is sparsely lit with candle light
and the husband and wife are eating in silence.

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:35.820
The only noise that can be heard is the tinkling
of cutlery as they cut their food.

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:40.870
Jane awkwardly looks at Paul and tries to
say something but decides against it.

00:00:40.870 --> 00:00:45.170
Throughout the dinner, she glances at him
several times trying to start any kind of

00:00:45.170 --> 00:00:47.710
conversation to end the awkwardness.

00:00:47.710 --> 00:00:51.260
Paul, on the other hand, hardly acknowledges
her.

00:00:51.260 --> 00:00:55.710
His entire focus is on his food that he seems
to be enjoying greatly.

00:00:55.710 --> 00:01:00.149
Having had enough of acting like strangers,
Jane wipes her hand and gets up.

00:01:00.149 --> 00:01:03.660
She picks up the bottle of wine on the table
and approaches her husband.

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:08.110
Jane hopes to stir up a conversation again
but as she tries to pour him the alcohol,

00:01:08.110 --> 00:01:10.390
he covers his glass with his palm.

00:01:10.390 --> 00:01:13.360
Jane is taken aback but she doesn’t react.

00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:17.530
Paul talks for the first time and claims that
he doesn’t want to drink.

00:01:17.530 --> 00:01:22.829
To sound a little less harsh he calls her
dear but it does not make Jane feel any better.

00:01:22.829 --> 00:01:27.439
She simply sits back down in her seat and
looks visibly hurt by her husband’s lack

00:01:27.439 --> 00:01:28.439
of concern.

00:01:28.439 --> 00:01:32.649
She talks for the first time and reveals that
it is their wedding anniversary, urging him

00:01:32.649 --> 00:01:35.200
to let go and drink on the occasion.

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:40.140
Hearing this, Paul stops eating and looks
her dead in the eyes, clearly annoyed by all

00:01:40.140 --> 00:01:43.579
the talking when he could be enjoying his
meal in silence.

00:01:43.579 --> 00:01:47.650
He simply says that he cannot drink because
he has to work the next day.

00:01:47.650 --> 00:01:52.050
When the husband doesn’t even bother to
explain further, Jane sighs of annoyance.

00:01:52.050 --> 00:01:56.630
To make up for him not drinking, she chugs
down an entire glass of wine while not breaking

00:01:56.630 --> 00:01:58.259
eye contact with him.

00:01:58.259 --> 00:02:02.150
She puts the glass down with a sigh, proud
of herself for rebelling.

00:02:02.150 --> 00:02:07.810
Still, Paul doesn’t utter a word to comment
on the fact, so she fills up the glass again.

00:02:07.810 --> 00:02:11.630
Before she can chug down the rest of it, Paul
states that the asparagus that she made for

00:02:11.630 --> 00:02:13.710
dinner is very tender.

00:02:13.710 --> 00:02:22.210
In a last attempt to stir up a spicy conversation,
Jane claims that people say asparagus is an

00:02:22.210 --> 00:02:26.640
aphrodisiac; a food that increases sexual
desire and pleasure.

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:31.250
The wife is hoping for an interesting reply
from him but is left disappointed when he

00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:33.110
asks her where she heard that from.

00:02:33.110 --> 00:02:36.140
She stammers and claims that she heard it
from some people.

00:02:36.140 --> 00:02:38.860
Jane appears to have gotten nervous after
the question.

00:02:38.860 --> 00:02:43.000
She quickly puts food in her mouth to keep
from talking but it doesn’t go unnoticed

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:44.020
by the husband.

00:02:44.020 --> 00:02:47.910
Paul doesn’t question her further and they
settle back to their old routine.

00:02:47.910 --> 00:02:52.220
Only a few seconds later, he calls her dear
and asks her about her day.

00:02:52.220 --> 00:02:54.270
This is the last straw for Jane.

00:02:54.270 --> 00:02:58.370
When the anger gets the best of her, she gets
up and throws her just filled glass of wine

00:02:58.370 --> 00:03:00.180
to Paul’s face.

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:04.940
Having enough of his nonchalant and uptight
behavior, she asks him to shut up and have

00:03:04.940 --> 00:03:06.430
a drink for once.

00:03:06.430 --> 00:03:11.600
She also comments that he is only a mere computer
analyst and not a surgeon so nothing is going

00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:15.450
to change if he drinks a glass of wine for
a special occasion.

00:03:15.450 --> 00:03:19.020
Throughout her screaming, Paul remains calm
and composed.

00:03:19.020 --> 00:03:22.360
The fact that his face is covered in wine
doesn’t seem to bother him as much.

00:03:22.360 --> 00:03:26.220
Jane again asks him to relax for once in his
life.

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:31.140
The husband ignores her entirely and brings
out his case of cigarettes to have a smoke.

00:03:31.140 --> 00:03:36.780
An already furious Jane glows red in anger
after seeing him put a cigarette to his mouth.

00:03:36.780 --> 00:03:40.750
She whispers to him to not dare smoke but
it doesn’t stop the husband.

00:03:40.750 --> 00:03:45.590
He lights the cigarette up and takes a big
puff making Jane get up and snatch the cigarette

00:03:45.590 --> 00:03:47.150
away from his lips.

00:03:47.150 --> 00:03:51.930
She claims that the house is hers, so he will
have to do what she wants.

00:03:51.930 --> 00:03:56.770
She presses the cigarette on an ashtray but
turns around to see that Paul has lit another

00:03:56.770 --> 00:03:57.770
one.

00:03:57.770 --> 00:04:01.690
The husband waits for another glass of wine
to his face but it never comes.

00:04:01.690 --> 00:04:06.800
To his utmost surprise, Jane composes herself
and sits down in her seat.

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:11.650
She sarcastically encourages him to keep going,
stating that passive smoke is exactly what

00:04:11.650 --> 00:04:13.690
she wanted as her anniversary gift.

00:04:13.690 --> 00:04:17.370
Paul doesn’t answer so she keeps talking
to fill the silence.

00:04:17.370 --> 00:04:21.239
Jane claims that she only gets the privilege
of stilted conversations with her husband

00:04:21.239 --> 00:04:22.680
on a normal day.

00:04:22.680 --> 00:04:27.060
She ironically adds that if she is extremely
lucky she might get a short mechanical sexual

00:04:27.060 --> 00:04:28.500
intercourse from him.

00:04:28.500 --> 00:04:33.820
The insult hurts Paul’s feelings and he
finally shows a hint of emotion on his face.

00:04:33.820 --> 00:04:38.410
He stares at her with teary eyes which brings
Jane back from her angered state.

00:04:38.410 --> 00:04:40.790
She regretfully apologizes for saying that.

00:04:40.790 --> 00:04:46.380
Moments later, she walks up to him and sits
on his lap trying to console him like a child.

00:04:46.380 --> 00:04:50.760
She claims that she didn’t mean what she
said but Paul is not naive to believe her

00:04:50.760 --> 00:04:51.760
words.

00:04:51.760 --> 00:04:55.410
Jane hugs him and slowly slides her hands
down the back of his head.

00:04:55.410 --> 00:05:00.190
One might think she is trying to seduce him,
but she turns off a switch on his neck.

00:05:00.190 --> 00:05:02.060
Paul goes limp after that.

00:05:02.060 --> 00:05:06.540
It is then revealed that he is actually a
robot that Jane has brought from a robotics

00:05:06.540 --> 00:05:09.790
company that provides AI boyfriend services.

00:05:09.790 --> 00:05:14.280
She sits back in her place, this time with
her feet on the dining table, and wishes her

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:16.560
former husband a happy anniversary.

00:05:16.560 --> 00:05:22.020
A while later, she is on her laptop browsing
for a new husband on the robotic company’s

00:05:22.020 --> 00:05:23.020
website.

00:05:23.020 --> 00:05:27.380
After looking for some time, she finds the
one she likes; a man who is athletic and way

00:05:27.380 --> 00:05:29.560
more interesting than the current one.

00:05:29.560 --> 00:05:34.310
She calls the company and complains that she
is unsatisfied with the model of man she owns.

00:05:34.310 --> 00:05:38.970
The operator apologizes for the inconvenience
and asks her what problems she is facing.

00:05:38.970 --> 00:05:44.120
Jane claims that Paul lacks ambition and has
no sense of adventure, he is just too much

00:05:44.120 --> 00:05:46.440
of a robot to be a good husband.

00:05:46.440 --> 00:05:50.050
The operator claims that lack of ambition
is a common malfunction with the series of

00:05:50.050 --> 00:05:52.120
robots that Paul belongs to.

00:05:52.120 --> 00:05:56.860
She asks Jane the features she would like
her updated husband to be incorporated with.

00:05:56.860 --> 00:06:02.570
Jane says that she wants a more athletic man
who either does rock climbing or is a masseuse.

00:06:02.570 --> 00:06:07.660
She looks at a reference photo and asks for
a man with less beard and shorter blonde hair.

00:06:07.660 --> 00:06:11.160
After providing all the information on what
she wants him to look like, Jane waits for

00:06:11.160 --> 00:06:13.790
the delivery that will happen the same night.

00:06:13.790 --> 00:06:16.780
Only some hours later, someone knows on her
door.

00:06:16.780 --> 00:06:20.830
She peeks through the looking hole to make
sure it is the people she was waiting for.

00:06:20.830 --> 00:06:25.510
She opens it to find a woman from the robotics
company standing outside.

00:06:25.510 --> 00:06:29.990
Seconds later, she is joined by another woman
with the box of her preferred husband.

00:06:29.990 --> 00:06:34.540
The workers take the new man out of the plastic
bag and place him on his seat at the dining

00:06:34.540 --> 00:06:35.540
table.

00:06:35.540 --> 00:06:40.570
Jane is left speechless after seeing his handsome
face, although he looks identical to the previous

00:06:40.570 --> 00:06:42.639
Paul, only a bit blonder.

00:06:42.639 --> 00:06:45.420
They put the old one in a stretcher and take
him out.

00:06:45.420 --> 00:06:50.190
However, Jane cannot help but stop them to
wish her former husband goodbye for the last

00:06:50.190 --> 00:06:51.190
time.

00:06:51.190 --> 00:06:56.080
She runs to him and gently kisses him on the
lips, regretful that she has to let him go,

00:06:56.080 --> 00:06:59.730
but happy that she has an upgraded husband
now.

00:06:59.730 --> 00:07:03.400
Following that, she pulls out the wedding
ring from his finger and lets the worker take

00:07:03.400 --> 00:07:04.430
him away.

00:07:04.430 --> 00:07:07.810
She then brings the ring inside and makes
her new husband wear it.

00:07:07.810 --> 00:07:12.060
The upgraded version of Paul is already fitted
with his old memories so Jane will not have

00:07:12.060 --> 00:07:15.720
to bother to introduce herself and take their
relationship from the start.

00:07:15.720 --> 00:07:20.840
She simply turns his switch on and continues
having dinner as she did with the former Paul.

00:07:20.840 --> 00:07:24.490
The upgraded Paul wakes up and eats his first
bite of food.

00:07:24.490 --> 00:07:27.389
Jane waits for him to say something but he
doesn’t.

00:07:27.389 --> 00:07:30.120
However, she doesn’t appear to be disappointed.

00:07:30.120 --> 00:07:34.840
She offers him a glass of wine but like the
previous Paul, this one also declines and

00:07:34.840 --> 00:07:38.050
claims that he has a big climb the next day.

00:07:38.050 --> 00:07:42.550
Proving how similar he is to the not upgraded
version, he also comments that the asparagus

00:07:42.550 --> 00:07:45.530
is very tender.

00:07:45.530 --> 00:07:50.950
However, something shifts in the conversation
following that.

00:07:50.950 --> 00:07:54.560
Jane starts to act submissive like the not
upgraded Paul did.

00:07:54.560 --> 00:07:59.090
She affirms that the vegetable is in fact
good and doesn’t continue the conversation.

00:07:59.090 --> 00:08:04.330
To spice up the conversation, the upgraded
Paul claims that asparagus is aphrodisiac.

00:08:04.330 --> 00:08:08.460
He expects her to reply to his comment with
something interesting, but just like the previous

00:08:08.460 --> 00:08:11.699
Paul, she asks him where he heard that from.

00:08:11.699 --> 00:08:14.340
She calls him dear and doesn’t converse
much.

00:08:14.340 --> 00:08:19.050
It is almost as if Paul is tired of her being
nonchalant to their wedding anniversary.

00:08:19.050 --> 00:08:21.660
Paul gets up from his seat and walks towards
her.

00:08:21.660 --> 00:08:25.330
Jane is nervous and confused as to what he
is about to do.

00:08:25.330 --> 00:08:29.400
He takes her by surprise and starts to seductively
massage her shoulders.

00:08:29.400 --> 00:08:32.930
As she melts in his touch, he asks her about
her day.

00:08:32.930 --> 00:08:37.700
The last time he asked her the same question
ended up in him being showered with wine,

00:08:37.700 --> 00:08:42.510
however, something has changed this time because
Jane is more nervous than angry.

00:08:42.510 --> 00:08:46.630
She replies to his question, saying that she
went to the town to get some stuff for dinner

00:08:46.630 --> 00:08:47.630
tonight.

00:08:47.630 --> 00:08:51.980
Jane can hardly focus on what she is trying
to say as Paul touches her appealingly.

00:08:51.980 --> 00:08:58.210
The stress she had from dealing with the older
one vanishes as she relaxes in his touch.

00:08:58.210 --> 00:09:04.120
He urges her to continue, so she explains
how she went out for lunch with her friend

00:09:04.120 --> 00:09:05.120
Anna.

00:09:05.120 --> 00:09:09.270
As she speaks, she cannot stop smiling at
the thought of having such a wonderful husband

00:09:09.270 --> 00:09:13.820
who gives her massages and is considerate
enough to ask her about her day.

00:09:13.820 --> 00:09:18.589
She continues to talk and proudly says that
she treated herself for the anniversary.

00:09:18.589 --> 00:09:23.030
One second, she is talking about her day and
the other, her expression changes and she

00:09:23.030 --> 00:09:24.250
stops abruptly.

00:09:24.250 --> 00:09:26.850
A click sound is heard from the back.

00:09:26.850 --> 00:09:29.680
Paul doesn’t react to his wife going limp.

00:09:29.680 --> 00:09:32.310
In contrast, he simply walks away.

00:09:32.310 --> 00:09:36.350
When the camera pans to the back of Jane’s
head, we see that she also has a switch on

00:09:36.350 --> 00:09:39.790
the back of her neck that Paul has just turned
off.

00:09:39.790 --> 00:09:43.190
Only then, it is revealed that she is also
a robot.

00:09:43.190 --> 00:09:47.670
The updated version of Paul was too advanced
for her, so he found her boring, similar to

00:09:47.670 --> 00:09:50.010
what she thought of the former Paul.

00:09:50.010 --> 00:09:54.140
This is the reason that all three of them
often repeated each other’s words and didn’t

00:09:54.140 --> 00:09:55.140
realize it.

00:09:55.140 --> 00:09:58.930
They were manufactured by the same company
which means that their primary behavior is

00:09:58.930 --> 00:09:59.930
the same.

00:09:59.930 --> 00:10:03.530
Paul simply sits on the couch with a lit cigarette
and a bottle of beer.

00:10:03.530 --> 00:10:07.430
He puts his feet on top of the coffee table
and turns the TV on.

00:10:07.430 --> 00:10:17.060
In the last scene, he stares into the television,
watching a football match.

